{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f22577767a7bc3e390d35be2a43c972d06f49a1447fb5e63f3f17e159e0025f1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nHere is the definition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:958ede3cc3da625cb57309ca857b03059c75dc19770cc85867efc26fd407d787", "unit_id": "tag:08LT:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0003": "$f : \\Sh(\\mathcal{D}) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$f_*$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-embedding}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:a4d7967806a19455d8e15dae2c07ffa16809a6775547da1cd27ddb7efef6067f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b7acfe7bd807475cf16ee01827c81bf781c4131cfc004764c928b54261fdcb5e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> be sites.\nA morphism of topoi <MATH_0003>\nis called an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>embedding<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if <MATH_0004> is fully faithful.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:80e18b4496c17662897ee30a4c5aa4952af1ad75d35aba803014ef6e51f6677c", "unit_id": "tag:08LU:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f^{-1}f_*\\mathcal{F} \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-exactness-properties}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f008345227a06508b303554e25ebf2d3edf4a4818a78eb7ef66ed3193c06b78b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:de0311477483685742ffa2e2f50d6542a021488e2cbf1b510e388fbf5c7f8d8e", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nAccording to Lemma <REF_0001>\nthis is equivalent to asking the\nadjunction map <MATH_0001>\nto be an isomorphism for every sheaf <MATH_0002> on <MATH_0003>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b53803c80c86d412bba9844211199775a447bd7419fa8413e18eb5fc473d0e79", "unit_id": "tag:08LT:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$E \\subset \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$f : \\Sh(\\mathcal{D}) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$E$", "MATH_0005": "$f_*$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-subtopos}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:03503c668784254e1796cf42d0486f13263244cf14651e79c60abd716d9bb06c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6a8f1b3827d2c675bd744a5f2a6b85e853eb07488baf22ceef4bb5e0c15e1848", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. A strictly full subcategory\n<MATH_0002> is a <TEXTITOPEN_0001>subtopos<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if there\nexists an embedding of topoi <MATH_0003>\nsuch that <MATH_0004> is equal to the essential image of the functor <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:621d51336a470dcc24bf6efc51ea5b8882d1e3772ee226ac6dbc8ad64cf7fcae", "unit_id": "tag:08LV:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f22577767a7bc3e390d35be2a43c972d06f49a1447fb5e63f3f17e159e0025f1", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe subtopoi constructed in the following lemma will be dubbed\n\"open\" in the definition later on.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3ea3868281bda80bf060a830a06957f174d750085f591174f44d799fcaf64ae3", "unit_id": "tag:08LT:prose-0003"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-open-subtopos}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:05b17352a3b41cadd154c5eb2f9d003153baa31a2c039f5dcc2c2a06fb895cba", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a56b50a2257dd81844887f43b5ce0d8c40bfb8c6ad9618f669b4a0d8c6d045ee", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be a sheaf on\n<MATH_0003>. The following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0004> is a subobject of the final object of\n<MATH_0005>, and\n<STRUCT_0003> the topos <MATH_0006> is a subtopos of\n<MATH_0007>.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:400bb81d0a4481755bdf1bf0d3ac804f1c6e08a4e7806dbd238759c78c71afe6", "unit_id": "tag:08LW:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$X$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{F} = h_U$", "MATH_0006": "$j_\\mathcal{F} : \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/\\mathcal{F} \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0007": "$j_U : \\Sh(\\mathcal{C}/U) \\to \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0008": "$j_U^{-1}j_{U, *}\\mathcal{G} \\to \\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{G}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0011": "$Z/U$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{C}/U$", "MATH_0013": "$$\n(j_{U, *}h_{Z/U})(U) = \\Mor_{\\mathcal{C}/U}(U \\times_X U/U, Z/U)\n$$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{G} = h_{Z/U}$", "MATH_0015": "$$\n\\Mor_{\\mathcal{C}/U}(U \\times_X U/U, Z/U) = \\Mor_{\\mathcal{C}/U}(U, Z/U)\n$$", "MATH_0016": "$Z/U$", "MATH_0017": "$U \\times_X U = U$", "MATH_0018": "$U \\to X$", "MATH_0019": "$j_U^{-1} j_{U, *} = \\text{id}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-localize-topos}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-topos-good-site}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-localize-topos}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{lemma-localize-given-products}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{categories-lemma-yoneda}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{categories-lemma-characterize-mono-epi}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-restrict-back}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0003": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0004": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:22826aeb33131d5d4931f4f56ca04e233e5479c4f3e1bd4e2fca30de62e70566", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:266339d94deca17daeabb1879488190dab50c2628af10b0df1849e86d255d468", "source_text": "We have seen in Lemma <REF_0001> that\n<MATH_0001> is a topos. In fact, we recall the\nproof. First we apply Lemma <REF_0002>\nto see that we may assume <MATH_0002> is a site with a subcanonical\ntopology, fibre products, a final object <MATH_0003>, and an object <MATH_0004> with\n<MATH_0005>. The proof of\nLemma <REF_0003>\nshows that the morphism of topoi\n<MATH_0006>\nis equal (modulo certain identifications) to the localization morphism\n<MATH_0007>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nAssume (2). This means that <MATH_0008>\nis an isomorphism for all sheaves <MATH_0009> on <MATH_0010>.\nFor any object <MATH_0011> of <MATH_0012> we have\n<MATH_0013>\nby Lemma <REF_0004>.\nSetting <MATH_0014> in the equality above we obtain\n<MATH_0015>\nfor all <MATH_0016>. By Yoneda's lemma\n(Categories, Lemma <REF_0005>)\nthis implies <MATH_0017>. By\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0006>\n<MATH_0018> is a monomorphism, in other words (1) holds.\n\n<STRUCT_0003><STRUCT_0004>\nAssume (1). Then <MATH_0019> by\nLemma <REF_0007>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6c3357c6691664402170cf0cd2a2ab1cb48f722667f006b16f56870ac848f287", "unit_id": "tag:08LW:proof"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$E \\subset \\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0005": "$E$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})/\\mathcal{F}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-open-subtopos}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-open-subtopos}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:db9d02052cb3e46a1ed9f25d13971a1f8c4f8de90db9637e78e02a1e304ae3aa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b94ad8739050f4e76eb338d205673ff293564676cd3b93339b3e11c22f1b8573", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. A strictly full subcategory\n<MATH_0002> is an <TEXTITOPEN_0001>open subtopos<TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nif there exists a subsheaf <MATH_0003> of the final object\nof <MATH_0004> such that <MATH_0005> is the subtopos\n<MATH_0006> described in Lemma <REF_0001>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:020628a957584f4f59bb8547595cb29e2cf97dc99421cc31759d5f2f0436d8e8", "unit_id": "tag:08LX:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "08LT", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:72df8f10f93993f803fb4212e5d1291bf9e1764d555a710618a93d0468d8ce75", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:88ea46132f2975c902e81d877f39baa561baee6edc5ad06f94e4a95fd01eda96", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis means there is a bijection between the collection of open subtopoi\nof <MATH_0001> and the set of subobjects of the final object of\n<MATH_0002>. Given an open subtopos there is a \"closed\" complement.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df8ad8a10d251f508fd2e470a3516914fc97d897b9474f76964912c93ed9f530", "unit_id": "tag:08LT:prose-0004"}
